In message <MnThd.2494$op3.104720@news.xtra.co.nz>, David Corbett wrote:
..
> Is there something preventing a player from having more then one game 
> > going (by that I mean can you save a character, and then start a new 
> > character) at one time?
> 
> You can't save and start a new character on the same server, since all 
> your characters automatically have the same name. You could play 
> characters on more than one server.

True.  What's actually being tracked is the order in which you _complete_ games.

It is possible to have games going on all 5 servers and to save and stop
playing right before you die in any of them without afecting the control
servers' concept of "consective".  It does give you a bit of wiggle room, but
not _too_ much.

It has been suggested that next year we restrict this to 13 consecutive games
on a single server, to guarantee that they're _actually_ consecutive, but that
may be overreacting.

